Moonsilence <usenetNO@JUNKmoonsilence.de> writes:
> Do food rations go bad with age, or are they either generated normal
> or rotten - and stay that way forever in the inventory until eaten? Or
> is it just by chance, that a food ration will be revealed as either
> fine or rotten upon eating? 

Any non-corpse food item other than fortune cookies that is older than
30 turns if uncursed, 50 turns if blessed, may be rotten (in general,
a flat 1/7 chance); if cursed, will always be. (Corpses other than
lizards or lichens may also be rotten, but the buc status and age
aren't important for this.  It's important for being tainted,
naturally.) Tins work slightly differently and more complicatedly.

> Since food rations are stackable items, can I assume that
> after eating a rotten food ration from a stack of several, that the
> next one will also be rotten?

The chance is per-item.

